# The three-Oblivion-Ring loop with Bot2 holding Disenchant and two untapped Plains, as in
# oblivion-ring-loop-a-player-can-break-with-an-instant-is-not-a-draw - but Bot2 never casts it. At every priority Bot2 could
# stop the loop, so it is no loop of mandatory actions and no draw by the rules (CR 104.4b's last sentence); and Disenchant
# is no part of the loop, so Bot2 can't be made to cast it (CR 732.5). The loop goes round for as long as Bot2 passes: a
# person is held to the match clock, and the engine ends a game whose history reaches its limit in a draw
# (docs/rules-exceptions.md, RX-1). The scenario sets that limit low; the game is a draw there, Disenchant still in Bot2's hand.

[Event Limit]
10000

[Bot1 Deck]
Oblivion Ring
Oblivion Ring
Oblivion Ring
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Plains
Disenchant
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Oblivion Ring.Cast
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Oblivion Ring.Cast
[T9 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Oblivion Ring.Cast

[Expect]
Result = Draw
DrawReason = EventLimit
Turn = 9
Step = Main1
Stack.Count = 1
Bot2.Battlefield = Plains; Plains
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains#1.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains#2.Tapped = false
Bot2.Hand = Disenchant; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island
Bot1.Status = (absent)
Bot2.Status = (absent)
